      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KATUNGA EXPRESS (2) had to work from a back row draw so did well to stick on and go under by 4m last start at Maryborough. Recorded back-to-back placings prior so has been going well. Has the benefit of a good draw. Big chance. SECRET SERVICE AGENT NZ (4) took on a Victoria Derby heat last start and tackled the Vicbred Super Series prior. This is the easiest race he has encountered since a Geelong win back in August so he is much better placed. POPCORNFRIDAY (1) was runner-up fresh then beaten only 2.4m here last start, both from back row barriers. Proven third-up so should be race fit and is better served by the ace draw. DONMARO NZ (10) will strip fitter second-up and is on the list of contenders if he has some luck from a tough draw.",
